 "text": "Why can't you quit someone who treats you badly? Blame a pigeon. In the 1950s, B.F. Skinner trained pigeons to peck for food. Food every time? They quit fast when it stopped. Food at random? They kept pecking. And pecking. Here's the trick. Random rewards are the most addictive. It's how slot machines work. And it's how manipulators hook people. Kind, cold, kind again. Still waiting for the good days to come back? That's the hook. Follow for more dark psychology.",
